# 2026-05-20 — TIL: use AbortController.signal with addEventListener to auto-clean listeners

A concise pattern to attach DOM/event listeners that can be cancelled in one call (avoids manual removeEventListener bookkeeping).

- addEventListener accepts an options object with `signal` (AbortSignal).
- Calling `controller.abort()` removes all listeners registered with that signal.

```js
// Attach multiple listeners and cancel them together
const controller = new AbortController();
const { signal } = controller;

button.addEventListener('click', onClick, { signal });
window.addEventListener('resize', onResize, { signal });

// Later: remove all of them in one go
controller.abort(); // all listeners registered with this signal are removed

function onClick(e) {
  console.log('clicked', e.target);
}
function onResize() {
  console.log('resized');
}

// Useful for components: abort on unmount/cleanup
function mountComponent(el) {
  const ctrl = new AbortController();
  el.addEventListener('mousemove', () => {}, { signal: ctrl.signal });
  return () => ctrl.abort(); // call during unmount
}
```

Note: widely supported in modern browsers; for older environments, polyfill or manual removeEventListener is needed.